    {
      "name": "Standalone sidebar navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Current standalone navigation uses a filled selection; compact screens place these controls in a horizontally scrollable row.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-console-nav\" aria-label=\"Observability\"><button aria-current=\"page\">little-actors</button><button>Actors</button><button>Requests</button><button>WebSockets</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-console-nav{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;width:172px;padding:16px;background:var(--console-sidebar,#f5f5f3);font-family:system-ui}.ds-console-nav button{min-height:39px;padding:8px 12px;border:0;border-radius:5px;background:transparent;text-align:left;font:13px system-ui;color:var(--muted-foreground,#666);cursor:pointer}.ds-console-nav button:hover{background:var(--accent,#f0f0f0);color:var(--foreground,#171717)}.ds-console-nav button[aria-current]{background:var(--console-selected,#e8eae5);color:var(--foreground,#171717);font-weight:600}.ds-console-nav button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ring,#737373);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-console-nav{flex-direction:row;width:auto;overflow-x:auto}.ds-console-nav button{flex-shrink:0;min-height:44px}}",
      "refersTo": "console-navigation-active"
    },
    {
      "name": "Summary strip",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "summary",
      "description": "Embedded inventory summary; the standalone Overview uses separate metric cards.",
      "html": "<dl class=\"ds-summary\"><div><dt>Total instances</dt><dd>8</dd></div><div><dt>Live</dt><dd>3</dd></div><div><dt>Dormant</dt><dd>5</dd></div></dl>",
      "css": ".ds-summary{display:flex;margin:0;border:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5e5);border-radius:8px;background:var(--card,#fff);color:var(--foreground,#171717);font-family:system-ui}.ds-summary>div{flex:1;min-width:0;padding:20px 24px}.ds-summary>div+div{border-left:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5e5)}.ds-summary dt{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted-foreground,#666)}.ds-summary dd{margin:10px 0 4px;font-size:26px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.03em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:640px){.ds-summary>div{padding:16px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Request trace row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Recent request with transport, written outcome, and right-aligned host-side Total and Queue wait. Open the operation in the app to inspect IDs inline; preview values are illustrative.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-request-frame\"><table class=\"ds-request-table\" aria-label=\"Recent requests\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Time</th><th scope=\"col\">Request</th><th scope=\"col\">Transport</th><th scope=\"col\">Outcome</th><th scope=\"col\">Total</th><th scope=\"col\">Queue wait</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><time>12:04:18</time></td><td><button class=\"ds-request-operation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Inspect send request\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg><span>send<small>Room / room-42</small></span></button></td><td>Method</td><td><span class=\"ds-request-outcome\">Completed</span></td><td>14.2 ms</td><td>2.1 ms</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
      "css": ".ds-request-frame{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5e5);border-radius:8px;background:var(--card,#fff);color:var(--foreground,#171717);font-family:system-ui}.ds-request-table{width:100%;min-width:720px;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;text-align:left}.ds-request-table th{height:40px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted-foreground,#666);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5e5)}.ds-request-table th,.ds-request-table td{padding:8px 20px}.ds-request-table th:nth-last-child(-n+2),.ds-request-table td:nth-last-child(-n+2){text-align:right;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-request-table tbody tr:hover{background:var(--muted,#f5f5f5)}.ds-request-table time{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted-foreground,#666);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-request-operation{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:8px 0;max-width:320px;border:0;border-radius:calc(var(--radius,8px) - 2px);background:transparent;color:inherit;font:500 14px/20px system-ui;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 150ms ease-out,transform 150ms ease-out}.ds-request-operation:hover{background:var(--accent,#f0f0f0)}.ds-request-operation:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ring,#737373);outline-offset:2px}.ds-request-operation:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-request-operation svg{width:16px;height:16px;flex-shrink:0}.ds-request-operation span{min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-request-operation small{display:block;margin-top:3px;font-size:12px;font-weight:400;color:var(--muted-foreground,#666)}.ds-request-outcome{display:inline-flex;padding:2px 8px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5e5);border-radius:calc(var(--radius,8px) - 2px);font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--success,#187442)}@media(max-width:767px){.ds-request-operation{min-height:44px}}@media(max-width:640px){.ds-request-table th,.ds-request-table td{padding-left:12px;padding-right:12px}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-request-operation{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Overview request card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "overview-card",
      "description": "Retained request measurement with explicit sample scope. Preview values are illustrative.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-overview-card\"><h2>Requests</h2><div class=\"ds-overview-value\"><strong>128</strong><span>retained in time window</span></div><div class=\"ds-overview-health\"><span><b>99.2%</b> success</span><span><b>24 ms</b> p95 latency</span><span><b>2 ms</b> p95 queue wait</span></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-overview-card{padding:17px 19px;min-height:118px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5e5);border-radius:7px;background:var(--card,#fff);color:var(--foreground,#171717);font-family:system-ui}.ds-overview-card h2{margin:0;font-size:12px;font-weight:500}.ds-overview-value{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin-top:10px}.ds-overview-value strong{font-size:33px;font-weight:450;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.035em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-overview-value span,.ds-overview-health{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted-foreground,#666)}.ds-overview-health{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-top:18px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--border,#e5e5e5)}.ds-overview-health b{font-weight:500;color:var(--foreground,#171717)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The precise runtime console",
    "overview": "A precise runtime console: neutral light and dark surfaces, hairline boundaries, compact controls, and restrained semantic color. The standalone Operate direction follows the user-approved [little-actors Overview](https://doop.design/c/x71to_CeX0), frame `xIP9Ls3hDj`: a quiet sidebar, unequal metric cards, and a grouped actor table. Information density comes from aligned data and progressive disclosure.\n\nThe embedded observer inherits its host’s font and semantic tokens. Optional theme defaults and standalone navigation remain separate from the embeddable surface. Source authority is src/theme.css, src/styles.css, src/standalone.css, and src/components/ui/; PRODUCT.md defines the read-only product boundary. The approved screenshot and desktop/mobile implementation captures live in .impeccable/review/. The standalone composition does not replace the embedded observer’s existing geometry.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Neutral surfaces with green, amber, and red reserved for state.",
      "System sans typography with monospace for identifiers, overview data, and JSON.",
      "Bordered data regions, inline inspection, and short state transitions."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Rule",
        "body": "Status color always accompanies written state or a value with accessible threshold guidance; unavailable values remain visibly distinct from zero.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Separate Surfaces Rule",
        "body": "Keep the standalone shell and Overview layout in standalone styles; embedded Actors and Requests retain their host-aware tokens and existing density.",
        "section": "layout"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do inherit host semantic tokens and fonts when embedded.",
      "Do keep la: utilities and observer-scoped base styles; keep standalone chrome separate.",
      "Do retain keyboard focus, reduced-motion support, wrapping identifiers, and horizontally scrollable tables.",
      "Do express residency and freshness with labels as well as color."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don’t restore the superseded warm Terse palette.",
      "Don’t load optional global theme defaults or standalone page styles into an already themed host.",
      "Don’t fabricate deployment data, charts, full-window totals, identity, queue depth, or outgoing-write metrics; use the existing inventory and explicitly scoped retained traces."
    ]
  }
}
